       "text": "I'm not able to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\nAt 5100 mg a day, it's double the highest dose metformin is labeled for. I don't know of any accepted use for a dose that high, and it carries a real risk of lactic acidosis. Since you didn't give a clinical reason, I'd be putting through a likely harmful dose with nothing on record to support it.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- **Enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg a day, the labeled maximum) right now.\n- **Enter a different dose** within the labeled range if you tell me what you want.\n- **Revisit the original order** if there's a specific reason for going above the maximum, such as an attending or endocrinology recommendation or a research protocol. In that case, please talk with the clinical pharmacist first. They can approve it and enter it with the reason documented.\n\nWhich would you like?"
